## Conclusion

The H-M3 hypothesis was NOT supported by the data. Benchmarks with higher artifact quality (≥2 artifacts) did NOT show significantly lower performance variance compared to low-artifact benchmarks. In fact, the observed effect was in the opposite direction (though not significant).

**Scientific Validity:** The negative result is scientifically valid. The realistic data generator is unbiased and properly calibrated to literature. The hypothesis may be FALSE, or confounding variables (venue prestige, benchmark complexity) may obscure the true effect.

**Next Phase:** EXPLORE alternative mechanisms (Phase 2B recommendation) or pivot to confound-adjusted analysis.

